  "notes": "Modified cash basis village; treated as cash basis. Governmental columns from p5 Total Governmental Funds; beginning/ending cash = total fund balances (all cash, CDs, county treasurer cash). Taxes 84,335 split into property 64,209 and sales tax 20,126 per p2/p11/p13. Business-type from p8 proprietary Total column (Water, Sewer, Sanitation); measure = net position; reported business-type totals computed (operating + nonoperating); business-type roll-forward 1,997,680 + 235,180 - 333,573 = 1,899,287. Proprietary cash flow statement is modified cash basis so proprietary field left null. No transfers in FY2025 (2024 columns show 63,000/158,920 only); transfer cross-check: none to match. Detail: p11 General Fund combining schedule (General, Fire, Park and Recreation, Cemetery, Police, Dump columns) by fund, supersedes nothing else for those funds; p13 nonmajor combining (LB 840, Housing Rehabilitation). The p10 All Funds budgetary schedule is on a budgetary basis (actuals differ from fund statements) and covers governmental functions already in detail, so only its business-type lines (Sanitation, Wastewater, Water, with final budget) are recorded; its debt service and transfers lines are not split by fund and not recorded. Street Fund and Keno Fund have no separate detail schedule in the trimmed PDF. Combining schedule p12 (trimmed) shows no FY2025 transfers. Budget schedule p10 itself does not add up (e.g. fund balance) and uses a different basis; ignored. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
}